CSR vs SSR: Complete Guide
CSR - Client-Side Rendering 🌐
Definition: The browser downloads a minimal HTML file and JavaScript bundle, then React renders the entire UI in the browser.

How CSR Works

1. Browser requests page from server
2. Server returns minimal HTML + JS bundle
3. Browser downloads and executes JavaScript
4. React builds the UI in the browser
5. Page becomes interactive
CSR Example (Traditional React App)

// index.html - What server sends
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <title>My App</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div id="root"></div>
    <script src="/bundle.js"></script>
  </body>
</html>

// React takes over in the browser
import React from 'react';
import ReactDOM from 'react-dom/client';
import App from './App';

const root = ReactDOM.createRoot(document.getElementById('root'));
root.render(<App />);
