Detailed Comparison
Rendering Location
Aspect	CSR	SSR
Where UI is built	Browser	Server
Initial HTML	Empty <div>	Fully rendered
JavaScript required	Yes, for anything to show	Yes, for interactivity
Performance Comparison

CSR Timeline:
[Request] → [Download JS] → [Execute JS] → [Render UI] → [Interactive]
    ↑           ↑               ↑             ↑            ↑
  100ms       500ms           200ms         100ms        Total: 900ms

SSR Timeline:
[Request] → [Server Renders] → [HTML Arrives] → [Display] → [Hydrate] → [Interactive]
    ↑            ↑                  ↑            ↑          ↑           ↑
  100ms        200ms              100ms        50ms       200ms      Total: 650ms
Code Examples
CSR Example (Create React App)

// App.js
import React, { useState, useEffect } from 'react';

function App() {
  const [users, setUsers] = useState([]);
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);

  useEffect(() => {
    // Fetch happens in BROWSER
    fetch('/api/users')
      .then(res => res.json())
      .then(data => {
        setUsers(data);
        setLoading(false);
      });
  }, []);

  if (loading) return <div>Loading...</div>; // Shows in browser

  return (
    <ul>
      {users.map(user => <li key={user.id}>{user.name}</li>)}
    </ul>
  );
}

export default App;
SSR Example (Next.js)

// pages/users.js
function Users({ users }) {
  // No loading state needed - data already here!
  return (
    <ul>
      {users.map(user => <li key={user.id}>{user.name}</li>)}
    </ul>
  );
}

export async function getServerSideProps() {
  // Fetch happens on SERVER
  const res = await fetch('https://api.example.com/users');
  const users = await res.json();

  return { props: { users } };
}

export default Users;
Pros and Cons
CSR Pros ✅
Cheaper hosting - Just static files (CDN)
Rich interactions - Smooth SPA experience
Less server load - Server just serves files
Easy deployment - Deploy anywhere (Netlify, Vercel, S3)
CSR Cons ❌
Slower initial load - Wait for JS to download
Poor SEO - Search engines see empty HTML
Blank page - No content until JS loads
Bad on slow devices - Heavy processing in browser
SSR Pros ✅
Faster initial paint - HTML shows immediately
Better SEO - Search engines see full content
Better performance on slow devices - Server does heavy lifting
Social media previews - Meta tags are rendered
SSR Cons ❌
Expensive hosting - Needs Node.js server
More server load - Renders on every request
Slower navigation - Full page reloads (traditional SSR)
Complex setup - More infrastructure needed
Other Rendering Strategies
SSG - Static Site Generation

// Next.js - Build-time rendering
export async function getStaticProps() {
  // Runs at BUILD TIME, not request time
  const data = await fetchData();
  return { props: { data } };
}
ISR - Incremental Static Regeneration

// Next.js - Static with periodic updates
export async function getStaticProps() {
  const data = await fetchData();
  return {
    props: { data },
    revalidate: 60, // Regenerate every 60 seconds
  };
}
React Server Components (RSC)

// Server Component - No JavaScript sent to browser
async function ServerComponent() {
  const data = await db.query('SELECT * FROM users');
  return <div>{data}</div>; // Rendered on server, HTML only sent
}
When to Use What?
Use CSR when:
Building dashboards/admin panels
Behind login (no SEO needed)
Heavy interactive applications
Budget constraints (cheaper hosting)
Use SSR when:
Public-facing content (blogs, e-commerce)
SEO is critical
Social media sharing matters
First contentful paint is priority
Use SSG when:
Content doesn't change often
Maximum performance needed
Marketing pages, documentation
